 "drivingQuestion": "From where do we know that blemished priests share in the offerings?",
 "outcome": "resolved",
 "outcomeNote": "source supplied from a baraita; its purpose is refined in the next unit",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "zevachim.102a.19",
   "daf": "102a",
   "sentenceId": 18,
   "he": "בַּעֲלֵי מוּמִין, בֵּין בַּעֲלֵי מוּמִין כּוּ׳. מְנָא הָנֵי מִילֵּי? דְּתָנוּ רַבָּנַן: ״כׇּל זָכָר״ – לְרַבּוֹת בַּעֲלֵי מוּמִין.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches: «Blemished» priests, «whether» they are temporarily «blemished» or permanently blemished, receive a share and partake of offerings, but do not sacrifice them. The Gemara explains: «From where are these matters» derived? «As the Sages taught» in a baraita: The verse states with regard to the meal offering: «“Every male» among the sons of Aaron shall eat it” (Leviticus 6:11). The phrase “every male” serves «to include blemished» priests."
  }
 ],
